 :premise-recorded-before-the-result
 {:the-two-halves-as-they-stand
  "F2 half: `structure Receipt` (mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:240-242)
   carries citesTextOrEdges and scoreAlone, so ConformantFind.f2Receipted states
   receipt PRESENCE only; slice 4's finding is that the blindness is in the
   CARRIER, since the misattributing and the faithful finder are EQUAL after
   erasure to today's FindResult
   (mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:186).
   F4 half: `structure FindResult` (mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:247-250)
   carries selected/receipts/absence and no zeroMass -- that field is on the ROW
   carrier FindReceiptRow (mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:252-259) --
   which is why F4 is a predicate over a finder's INPUTS and not a conjunct of
   ConformantFind, and slice 5's finding is that its three readings form a
   lattice in which C is strictly stronger than B and A is incomparable with C
   in both directions."
  :expected-interaction
  "EXPECTED: the two halves are not independent, and the dependence runs one way.
   Adding the zero-mass designation to what `find` RETURNS internalises reading A
   and only reading A -- A is the reading in which the excluded pattern comes
   from the finder's own output, and a field the finder fills is by construction
   the finder's own nomination. Reading C takes the designation from OUTSIDE the
   finder (mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:26-29), so no field on
   FindResult can carry it, and reading B takes it from the record. So the carrier
   amendment is expected to buy F4-as-a-conjunct at the price of fixing F4 at its
   weakest reading, which is the one slice 5 measured as incomparable with the
   deontic one. If instead a FindResult field can carry C without the finder
   nominating, the expectation is refuted and THAT is the slice's finding.
   Written before the work so it cannot be back-fitted."
  :expected-subadditive-cost
  "EXPECTED: the joint cost is strictly less than the sum of the halves on the
   regeneration leg and equal to the sum on the proof leg. The contract authority
   is derived as `git log -1 -- Holes.lean`
   (mathlib4 DarkTower/Contract/Emit.lean:52-62), so an amendment to Receipt and
   an amendment to FindResult in the same file pay the C176 regeneration ONCE, not
   twice; and slice 4's edit-site census (7 construction sites, ONE outside the
   pricing modules) is expected to be the SAME 7 for the joint amendment rather
   than 7+n, because FindResult.receipts is typed by Receipt and the sites that
   build one build the other. If the joint census is larger than the F2 census,
   the expectation is refuted and the number is the measurement."
  :expected-non-buy
  "EXPECTED: the joint amendment does NOT buy a find that finds something. Slice 5
   proved every reading admits a conformant finder that finds nothing, C for every
   designation (mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:323-343). The
   amended carrier is expected to admit one too, so the sixth arm is expected to
   share the limit every other arm has. This is asked as a measurement because it
   is what stops the arm from being priced as a fix for the thing it does not fix."}
